From: Maciej Krüger <mkg20001@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:22:26 +0000
Subject: mmfd, l3roamd: fix the build on openwrt-25.12

CMake 4 refuses cmake_minimum_required below 3.5, and GCC 14 rejects the
positional msghdr initializer in l3roamd's routemgr.c on musl. Both
projects already carry the fixes in the ffgraz forks; until upstream
tags them, apply them as package patches.

diff --git a/net/l3roamd/patches/0001-raise-CMake-minimum-version.patch b/net/l3roamd/patches/0001-raise-CMake-minimum-version.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bacf8a2bada53a11b8d08706f05d5bed532a5277
--- /dev/null
+++ b/net/l3roamd/patches/0001-raise-CMake-minimum-version.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+From 0e6588caa0c96520ed802857050e4025096fff52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Maciej=20Kr=C3=BCger?= <mkg20001@gmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 03:21:54 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] raise CMake minimum version
+
+CMake 4 removed compatibility with CMake < 3.5, so the build fails at
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8.3).
+---
+ CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
+ 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
+index ea89942..34831c1 100644
+--- a/CMakeLists.txt
++++ b/CMakeLists.txt
+@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
+-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8.3)
++cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)
+ project(L3ROAMD C)
+ 
+ INCLUDE(FindPkgConfig)
diff --git a/net/l3roamd/patches/0002-use-designated-initializers-for-msghdr.patch b/net/l3roamd/patches/0002-use-designated-initializers-for-msghdr.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c393bf06054e12726139ad600fc36506d61410da
--- /dev/null
+++ b/net/l3roamd/patches/0002-use-designated-initializers-for-msghdr.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+From 6559c7053bc23f278943c94c250430b10c888dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Maciej=20Kr=C3=BCger?= <mkg20001@gmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 03:21:54 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] use designated initializers for msghdr
+
+The positional initializer assumes struct msghdr has exactly seven
+members in a fixed order, but musl places padding members between
+them, so NULL ends up initializing an int. GCC 14 rejects that with
+-Wint-conversion as an error.
+---
+ src/routemgr.c | 7 ++++++-
+ 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/routemgr.c b/src/routemgr.c
+index 117e4cb..6c4cb10 100644
+--- a/src/routemgr.c
++++ b/src/routemgr.c
+@@ -620,7 +620,12 @@ void rtmgr_rtnl_talk(int fd, struct nlmsghdr *req) {
+ 	struct sockaddr_nl nladdr = {.nl_family = AF_NETLINK};
+ 
+ 	struct iovec iov = {req, 0};
+-	struct msghdr msg = {&nladdr, sizeof(nladdr), &iov, 1, NULL, 0, 0};
++	struct msghdr msg = {
++		.msg_name = &nladdr,
++		.msg_namelen = sizeof(nladdr),
++		.msg_iov = &iov,
++		.msg_iovlen = 1,
++	};
+ 
+ 	iov.iov_len = req->nlmsg_len;
+ 
diff --git a/net/mmfd/patches/0001-raise-CMake-minimum-version.patch b/net/mmfd/patches/0001-raise-CMake-minimum-version.patch
